---
title: How to share a file discussion
sidebar:
  order: 7
---
To share a file within a discussion, follow these steps:

1. **Navigate to the Discussion Section**
   - On the left-hand sidebar, click on **Discussion** to access all your conversations.
1. **Select the Relevant Discussion**
   - From the list of discussions, select the conversation where you want to share the file.
1. **Access the File Attachment Option**
   - At the bottom-left corner of the message input box, click on the **paperclip icon** to open the file attachment option.
1. **Upload the File**
   - Choose the file you wish to share from your local storage. Once uploaded, the file will be displayed in the chat area with its name and size.
1. **View the Shared File**
   - The shared file will also appear in the **Files** tab at the top-right corner of the discussion, allowing all participants to easily view and download the attachment.

By following these simple steps, you can effectively share and manage files within your discussion threads.

## How Different File Types Appear in the Chat

Taskip renders each attachment differently depending on what it is, so you can preview it without downloading first:

- **Images** show as an inline thumbnail. Clicking one opens a full-size gallery viewer you can page through, covering every image in that message.
- **Video and audio** files get an inline player with playback controls, right in the message, so you can watch or listen without leaving the conversation.
- **PDF, Word, and PowerPoint** files that Taskip can generate a preview for show as a larger card with a page-one preview image, the file name, its size, and a download button.
- **Any other file type** shows as a compact icon with its file name, which you can click to open in the file viewer or download.
